AP68030: the register file in LUT RAM (Intel MLAB) - not applied

D0-D7 and A0-A6 move from flip-flops behind five 15-way read multiplexers
into MLABs (synchronous write, asynchronous read: the same timing), one copy
per read port, with a flag per register so it reads 0 from reset until first
written, as the reset to 0 did.  A bench view (rf.r[n]) stays for
tb_ap030_program.  Nothing else changes: the AP68030 regression passed in
the pin and native-port builds, and the Falcon core's benches with it.

Quartus 17.0, Falcon core: the register file 776 ALMs -> 464 (the whole core
333 fewer in a fit with only this change).  Kept as a patch, not a pull
request: the core fits without it (docs/CPU_TIMING.md, milestone 4).

Applies to AP68030 from the clock-enable commit (971cd22) on:
    cd rtl/AP68030 && git apply ../../extra/ap68030_regfile_mlab.patch

